FerrionOS change to userutils (MIT license, kept), made against upstream commit 641a5aa81574db79d883151bc3438d3e59f90b88 with ferrion-login-name.patch and ferrion-login-namespace.patch applied (issue 10):
- sudo no longer panics when standard output is not a terminal: it first hands the daemon an empty password, which the daemon accepts only for a member of group sudo whose password is empty in the account database (the policy login already follows), so such an account runs the command without a prompt;
- any other member is asked on the terminal that is standard input, with the prompt on standard error; when standard input is not a terminal sudo refuses with a message and exit status 1 and reads nothing from it;
- the daemon answers EACCES for a caller outside group sudo, which sudo reports at once, and refuses an empty password for an account that has one without the wrong-password delay; any other daemon error is a message and exit status 1 instead of a panic.

